# Settings every module of this repository imports from its .bazelrc.

# Fetch the source archives of Bazel Central Registry modules from the BCR's mirror before
# their GitHub URLs, as Bazel's own repository does; the registry's hashes verify them.
common --module_mirrors=https://bcr.cloudflaremirrors.com

# Path mapping gives actions that do not depend on the target configuration one cache key
# in every configuration: the dexing and desugaring of Android libraries, the Godot actions
# rules_godot opts in, such as the imports and validations of a project's units, which a
# host test and an Android or macOS application share, and the native and define-analysis
# actions of source-built engines, which applications with different build profiles share.
# Only the engines' targets opt their C++ actions in. Other actions keep their paths:
# path-mapped Java compilations of tools miss the local action cache on every build, and
# rules_go's standard library build fails.
common --experimental_output_paths=strip
common --modify_execution_info=(?!DexBuilder$|Desugar$|Godot|CppCompile$|CppArchive$|CppLink$|ObjcCompile$|DefineAnalysis$).*=-supports-path-mapping

# Python binaries get no implicit __init__.py files, the coming default of rules_python, also
# in modules that do not opt in through explicit_init_py, such as rules_apple, rules_android
# and Bazel's tools, which otherwise warn per tool in every build.
common --incompatible_default_to_explicit_init_py

# Actions run on this host unless a config such as --config=buildbuddy names remote execution
# platforms. --config=host-execution restores this host after such a config, because a later
# --extra_execution_platforms replaces earlier ones. Toolchains without execution constraints
# that resolve binaries of this host use it, such as the formatters of rules_multirun and
# rules_multitool that `bazel run` starts here. The default names the host as well, so the
# config changes no option without a remote config and keeps Bazel's analysis cache.
# Bazel resolves a flag's label in each module's own repository mapping, which need not include
# @platforms; every module sees @bazel_tools, whose host platform is an alias of @platforms//host.
common --extra_execution_platforms=@bazel_tools//tools:host_platform
common:host-execution --extra_execution_platforms=@bazel_tools//tools:host_platform

# --config=ci fails a command when the module's MODULE.bazel.lock is stale, rather than rewrite
# it. Only the root module and the ruleset check theirs in; CI's lanes set the config for
# every command there through ci.bazelrc (.github/workflows/ci.yml), since a server whose
# lockfile mode changes reloads every package. `aspect generate` regenerates the files.
common:ci --lockfile_mode=error

# Print the logs of failing tests, which CI does not keep.
test --test_output=errors

# Source-built editors for a debugger: --config=editor-debug compiles them in Bazel's dbg mode,
# as rules_godot's docs/public/engine.md describes. Editors build in the execution
# configuration, which keeps a custom flag only when it is propagated.
common:editor-debug --@autoload_rules_godot//godot:editor_debug
common:editor-debug --experimental_propagate_custom_flag=@autoload_rules_godot//godot:editor_debug

# The lint check of Python, which fails a build or test on Ruff's and ty's findings
# (tools/lint/check.bzl); builds without it ignore them. Only modules that depend on the root
# module use it, not the registry test modules.
common:check --aspects=@autoload_dev//tools/lint:check.bzl%python
# The lint check of the filegroups that Gazelle declares per package (tools/gazelle/lint): gdlint
# and rumdl, and the convention rules that judge each file on its own (tools/conventions/files.py).
# Those filegroups are no tests, so it needs a build that names them, such as the lint work's
# `--output_groups=lint_checks` over every target, or one with `--config=sources`, which
# builds only them; tag filters keep the analysis.
common:check --aspects=@autoload_dev//tools/lint:check.bzl%sources
build:sources --build_tag_filters=cc,gdscript,markdown,python_files,starlark

# The test tiers of `aspect tests` (.aspect/develop.axl). fast: every test but those that
# start a Godot process (RG026), the smoke tests included, which `aspect check` and the
# pre-push hook run; the ruleset's source-engine tests stay out, as its .bazelrc's default
# filter keeps them. all: every test this host can run.
test:fast --build_tests_only
test:fast --test_tag_filters=-godot_process,-source_engine
test:all --build_tests_only
